==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Crimson Mina''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Awakened Mina''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP after completing [[Eldritch Forces]].

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
Red Riding Mina is a very useful long-range attacker, one of the few non-[[:Category:Gacha Cats|gacha]] units that can snipe enemies such as [[Calamary]], [[Professor A.]] and [[Rain D.]] from behind the frontlines. Unfortunately her health and attack power in her Normal/Evolved Form pales in comparison to similar [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]]/[[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rares]], which means that you will mostly only use her in [[Restriction Stage]]s, unless you happen to encounter a stage where you are able to stack Minas at the beginning; most specifically, you will stack her behind your own [[Cat Base]], usually with the support of [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|Crowd-Controllers]] like [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Magica Cat]] or [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Prof. Cat Jobs]].

==='''True Form'''===
Awakened Mina gains a higher effective range, double damage, 1.5x more health and the ability to weaken [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]], albeit with a 50% chance. As specifically anti-Relic abilities are uncommon outside of [[Talents]], the niche in and of itself is important, as it allows her to counter dangerous enemies like [[Othom]] and [[M. Ost]]. So, whenever she does weaken, it can change the tide of the battle, as it helps [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Modern Cat]] and your other meatshields survive for longer. With this new addition, stacking her is even more important as it increases her chances to weaken to almost guaranteed!  However, if you have [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]' Talents, you'll likely rely on them for weaken instead of Mina as they're far more disposable.

Weaken aside, unlocking this form doubles her DPS and increases her piercing range to 265. Overall, she is a worthy use of your [[Catfruit|Elder Catfruit]], and is useful and relevant in numerous stages until [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] can be unlocked. With all this being said, do not let any enemies enter her blind spot unless you are trying to stack her, as most opponents encountered this late deal extremely high damage even on 1-Crown difficulty, and Mina has no abundance of health to safely tank any dangerous hits.

